WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:06.200
From exciting blockbusters to thought-provoking
indies, 2017 was a great year for films.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:11.090
And while audiences saw no shortage of great
moments on the big screen, plenty of quality

00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:14.010
scenes ended up on the cutting room floor.

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:18.740
Here are the best deleted scenes that you
probably missed in 2017.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:21.260
Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:26.260
Peter Quill may have saved the galaxy a few
times, but that doesn't make him an expert

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:28.770
on Earth's more primitive technology.

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:33.660
This deleted scene from Guardians of the Galaxy
Vol. 2 shows our intergalactic hero trying

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:35.980
to figure out how to work a Zune.

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:40.610
Kraglin, played by Sean Gunn, offers up some
rather choice musical opinions.

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:42.800
"Thin Lizzy is a group I like a lot.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:45.420
There's a lady on there named Alice Cooper
that I like a lot.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:49.780
She seems kinda angry, but it kinda like stuff
we felt like when we were kids."

00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:54.820
It makes sense that this slow scene would
be cut from the action-heavy outing, but this

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:58.300
funny character moment is still a must-see.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:00.010
Beauty and the Beast

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:05.940
One of the most bizarre plot points in Disney's
live action Beauty and the Beast has to do

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:09.970
with the castle staff, who have all been turned
into household items because of a curse.

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:14.220
A deleted scene from the recent live-action
remake of the film reveals what happened to

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:16.110
one of the castle's lesser servants.

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:21.750
We first meet the unfortunately named Monsieur
Toilette when Josh Gad's LeFou is scared away

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.610
by his gurgling voice.

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:28.390
In a deleted scene, after the curse has been
broken, LeFou notices a dirty, disheveled

00:01:28.390 --> 00:01:30.960
man who smells… rather familiar.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:35.200
"So what are you gonna do now?"

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:37.360
"Brush my teeth."

00:01:38.150 --> 00:01:43.240
Disgusting, but also very funny—especially
for fans of toilet humor.

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:45.210
Spider-Man: Homecoming

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:50.680
Even though fresh-faced Tom Holland was outstanding
as Peter Parker, some comic fans were hoping

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:56.460
to see someone else under the mask in Spider-Man:
Homecoming--namely, Miles Morales, the fan

00:01:56.460 --> 00:02:01.660
favorite comic book character who became the
Spider-Man of Marvel's Ultimate universe.

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:06.979
In Homecoming, Donald Glover plays Aaron Davis,
who is Miles's uncle in the comics.

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:09.100
"Hey that's gonna dissolve in two hours."

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:10.280
"No, no, no.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:11.520
Come fix this."

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:12.260
"Two hours.

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:14.460
You deserve that, you're a criminal."

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:19.520
While he merely hints at having a nephew in
the theatrical cut, Davis actually calls him

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:22.110
by name in an awesome deleted scene.

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:27.200
After Spider-Man webs his hand to his car,
Aaron, unable to release himself, eventually

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:28.940
gives in and calls his nephew.

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:30.210
"Yeah, sorry Miles.

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:32.200
I'm not gonna make it.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:33.760
Yeah I'm just stuck."

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:39.650
Although it's just a small reference, it was
more than enough to send comic book fans into

00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:40.720
a tizzy.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:42.530
Thor: Ragnarok

00:02:42.530 --> 00:02:47.480
The Hulk punching Thor was one of the most
memorable moments from The Avengers, and Thor:

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:50.670
Ragnarok almost included a callback to the
scene.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:56.030
As the team returned to Asgard, the Hulk was
originally supposed to punch Loki out of frame.

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:57.030
"Loki!

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:57.680
Loki's alive!

00:02:57.680 --> 00:02:58.820
Can you believe it?

00:02:58.820 --> 00:02:59.340
He's up there.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:00.500
Loki!

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:01.180
Look who it is!"

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:07.560
Considering what happened the last time these
two characters saw each other, it would have

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:09.750
been a hilarious reunion.

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:14.600
Director Taika Waititi revealed in an interview
with Empire that the much-loved moment had

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:15.600
to be cut for time.

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:18.810
"There's so many little things that yeah we've
had to get rid of for time.

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:23.190
And just sometimes it's like we have to choice
between that and Banner falling off the bridge

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:24.280
for the big laugh."

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:28.290
There are still plenty of other hilarious
moments in Thor: Ragnarok, but an Avengers

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:32.220
callback that also cut Loki down to size would
have been a fun addition.

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:35.849
Fingers crossed that it winds up on the DVD.

00:03:35.849 --> 00:03:37.160
Get Out

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:42.310
While Rose is clearly a villain in the film
Get Out, one deleted scene may make you question

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:44.530
everything you thought you knew about her.

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:50.100
When Chris, played by Daniel Kaluuya, describes
the Sunken Place to her, Rose reveals that

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:52.030
she, too, has had a similar experience.

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:53.590
"I had the same thing.

00:03:53.590 --> 00:03:56.010
She hypnotized me when I was in high school
for stage fright.

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:57.910
And I had the craziest nightmares.

00:03:57.910 --> 00:04:01.819
But I just remember thinking, it worked."

00:04:01.819 --> 00:04:06.400
Rose easily could have been lying to keep
Chris calm, but it raises the possibility

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:11.410
that she could also have been hypnotized into
cooperating with her family's evil plan.

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:15.540
Considering how it distracts from the film's
message and shows a truly evil character in

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:19.469
a sympathetic new light, it's easy to see
why the scene was cut.

00:04:19.469 --> 00:04:23.139
Still, it's interesting to consider the new
questions it would have raised if it had been

00:04:23.139 --> 00:04:25.280
kept in the film.

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:26.389
Logan

00:04:26.389 --> 00:04:32.350
There were so many deaths in Logan that some
characters, like Stephen Merchant's Caliban,

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:34.430
didn't even get to die on screen.

00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:40.279
A deleted scene, however, actually shows the
emotional demise of this fan favorite character.

00:04:40.279 --> 00:04:45.520
On the movie's Blu-ray commentary, Director
James Mangold explained that, while he felt

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:49.639
bad for cutting the scene, he didn't want
to call into question why Logan didn't just

00:04:49.639 --> 00:04:53.349
take Caliban's body with him like he did for
Professor X.

00:04:53.349 --> 00:04:57.419
Although the movie was plenty bleak without
an additional death scene, it would have been

00:04:57.419 --> 00:05:00.389
nice to have closure for such an important
character.

00:05:00.389 --> 00:05:04.509
Pirates of the Caribbean: Dead Men Tell No
Tales

00:05:04.509 --> 00:05:09.300
It may not have reached the seafaring heights
of the franchise's previous films, but Pirates

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:14.419
of the Caribbean: Dead Men Tell No Tales was
an undeniably fun addition to the saga of

00:05:14.419 --> 00:05:15.639
Jack Sparrow.

00:05:15.639 --> 00:05:20.259
This is most apparent in a deleted scene,
where Johnny Depp's freewheeling pirate finds

00:05:20.259 --> 00:05:23.759
himself at odds with Henry, the son of Will
Turner.

00:05:23.759 --> 00:05:26.400
"I saw her ankles."

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:28.919
"You'd see a lot more if you'd just keep your
cakehole shut."

00:05:28.919 --> 00:05:33.740
The clip begins with Henry threatening Jack
to help him break his father's curse.

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:39.250
In return, Jack helpfully offers the boy some
advice on how to hold his sword before demanding

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:40.419
to be run through.

00:05:40.419 --> 00:05:42.139
"Your first murder…

00:05:42.139 --> 00:05:43.740
Happy to be a part of it.

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:47.059
Just dont mind all the blood and all the bulging
eyeballs and such."

00:05:47.059 --> 00:05:51.900
Of course, having no intention of actually
letting Henry kill him, Jack pulls a gun on

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:52.900
him.

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:57.199
Luckily for audiences, both characters got
the chance to live another day on the high

00:05:57.199 --> 00:05:59.029
seas.

00:05:59.029 --> 00:06:00.569
The Breakfast Club

00:06:00.569 --> 00:06:05.479
It's been more than 30 years since The Breakfast
Club hit theaters, but fans of the original

00:06:05.479 --> 00:06:10.639
teenage misfits were treated to a deleted
scene thanks to the film's 2017 Criterion

00:06:10.639 --> 00:06:12.439
Collection deluxe reissue.

00:06:12.439 --> 00:06:17.360
The sequence kicks off in the girl's bathroom,
with Molly Ringwald's Claire expresses confusion

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:21.059
about Ally Sheedy's Allison and her particular
cleanliness habits.

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:24.400
"You wash your hands but you'll eat food inches
away from a live toilet?"

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:30.759
"I'm sorry, I don't wanna depress you."

00:06:30.759 --> 00:06:35.499
Allison stays predictably silent, and then
deliberately drops a potato chip in the sink

00:06:35.499 --> 00:06:37.479
before popping it into her mouth.

00:06:37.479 --> 00:06:41.449
Although the scene doesn't amount to much,
it's a welcome and fun interaction between

00:06:41.449 --> 00:06:42.960
two classic characters.

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:50.000
"This is not correct…"

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:52.219
Thanks for watching!

00:06:52.219 --> 00:06:54.779
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:54.779 --> 00:06:57.639
Plus, check out this other cool stuff we know
you'll love too!

